Domain-Driven Design (inspired-by per ADR-003 §2.4)
Source 1: Eric Evans, "Domain-Driven Design: Tackling Complexity in the
          Heart of Software" (Addison-Wesley, 2003)
Source 2: Vaughn Vernon, "Implementing Domain-Driven Design"
          (Addison-Wesley, 2013)

The ubiquitous-language concept (a shared vocabulary across code,
documentation, and domain experts) is referenced by
plugin/skills/audit-ubiquitous-language/PROCEDURE.md. The skill draws
the 3-source consistency frame (code identifier / PRD vocabulary /
domain business term) from these works and adapts the analysis primitives
(mismatch_type taxonomy: synonym/typo/abbreviation/translation/stale_legacy,
severity classification, bounded-context-scoped audit) to buddy's
PROCEDURE.md format. No verbatim text, code, or example was adopted;
the implementation is independently authored in buddy voice.
